[%# The runner recipes.yaml, dumped whole by the yaml formatter.

    A formatter rather than anything written here: a recipes.yaml is an
    arbitrarily deep structure that a template has no business trying to indent
    correctly, and Provisioner::Recipe::formatters is the hook for exactly this.

    Every store: reference in it comes out as a secret: on the way through, so
    what lands here names entries in the runner own keepass database and holds
    no passwords.  See SECRETS IN recipes in Provisioner::Recipe::trogrunner. -%]
[% recipes | yaml %]
